            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for applicability, then the Kannada for overall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಆಶಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಶಿಸು — āśisu — \"to hope for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಗ ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಸಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ ಅಂತ ತಾಯಿ ಆಶಿಸಿದಳು. maga parīkṣeyalli pāsāguttāne anta tāyi āśisidaḷu. The mother hoped her son would pass the exam."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಆಶಿಸಿದೆ, āśiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is hoped comes before ಅಂತ or ಎಂದು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಶಿಸು (āśisu) is built on Sanskrit āśā, \"wish, desire, hope\" (Monier-Williams), with the Kannada verb ending -isu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
